.Sh DESCRIPTION
A libdtfl record is a byte string.
A
.Vt dtfl_type
descriptor says how long a value is, how two values compare, how a
value hashes for exchange, and how to print one.
The library never interprets record bytes itself; it calls the
descriptor.
A descriptor's
.Fa cmp
must reproduce the derived
.Vt Ord
of the Rust type it models, because operators such as reduce hand
values to user code in that order.
.Pp
The built-in descriptors are static.
Their encodings are written and read with
.Xr dtfl_put_u64 3
and its siblings:
.Bl -tag -width "dtfl_type_string()"
.It Fn dtfl_type_unit
.Vt () :
zero bytes; every value is equal.
.It Fn dtfl_type_u8 No to Fn dtfl_type_u64
Unsigned integers, big-endian, 1 to 8 bytes.
.It Fn dtfl_type_i8 No to Fn dtfl_type_i64
Signed integers, big-endian with the sign bit flipped, so that
.Xr memcmp 3
order is numeric order.
.It Fn dtfl_type_bytes , Fn dtfl_type_string
.Vt Vec<u8>
and
.Vt String :
a u64 big-endian length, then the payload.
Values compare lexicographically over the payload, then by length, so
.Qq ab
<
.Qq abc
<
.Qq b .
This is not
.Xr memcmp 3
of the encoding, which would order by length first.
.El
.Pp
Composite descriptors are reference counted.
Each holds a reference to the descriptors it was built from, so the
caller may free those right away.
.Bl -tag -width "dtfl_type_option()"
.It Fn dtfl_type_tuple
The fields' encodings concatenated, compared field by field.
Every field except the last must delimit itself (fixed size or a
.Fa len
callback).
A tuple whose fields are all fixed size is fixed size.
.Fn dtfl_type_pair
is the two-field tuple; key and value collections use it.
.It Fn dtfl_type_option
A tag byte, 0 for
.Dv None
and 1 for
.Dv Some ,
then the value.
.Dv None
sorts before every
.Dv Some .
.It Fn dtfl_type_vec
A u64 big-endian count, then the elements, compared element by element
and then by count, as Rust's
.Vt Vec
.Vt Ord .
.El
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_type_new
copies a caller-defined descriptor into a reference-counted one.
.Fa def->internal
must be zero, and
.Fa def->name
must outlive the result.
When the last reference goes away,
.Fa def->ctx_free ,
if set, is called with
.Fa def->ctx .
.Fn dtfl_type_retain
adds a reference and returns its argument;
.Fn dtfl_type_free
drops one.
Both are no-ops for the built-ins and for
.Dv NULL .
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_type_cmp
compares two values and returns -1, 0 or 1.
A descriptor with no
.Fa cmp
compares with
.Xr memcmp 3
over the common prefix, then by length.
On malformed values the result is still a deterministic total order,
and no byte outside the given spans is read.
.Fn dtfl_type_hash
returns the descriptor's
.Fa hash ,
or 64-bit FNV-1a of the record bytes.
.Fn dtfl_type_fmt
prints a value the way Rust's
.Vt Debug
does: integers in decimal, strings quoted and escaped, tuples as
.Ql (a, b) ,
options as
.Ql None
or
.Ql Some(x) ,
and vectors as
.Ql [a, b] .
Bytes values and anything malformed print as hex.
.Fn dtfl_type_value_len
returns the length of the value that starts at
.Fa p ,
reading at most
.Fa avail
bytes.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_type_tuple_len
and
.Fn dtfl_type_tuple_field
return a tuple descriptor's arity and its
.Fa i Ns 'th
field.
.Fn dtfl_type_tuple_offset
locates field
.Fa i
in the tuple value
.Fa p
of
.Fa len
bytes and stores the field's length in
.Fa *flen .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The constructors return a descriptor that the caller releases with
.Fn dtfl_type_free .
.Fn dtfl_type_value_len
and
.Fn dtfl_type_tuple_offset
return
.Dv SIZE_MAX
if the bytes are not a valid value; 0 is a valid length.
.Fn dtfl_type_fmt
returns the number of characters written, or a negative value on an
output error.
.Sh EXAMPLES
A
.Vt (String, i64)
record:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
const dtfl_type *t = dtfl_type_pair(dtfl_type_string(),
    dtfl_type_i64());
unsigned char buf[64];
size_t n = dtfl_put_bytes(buf, "apple", 5);
size_t off, flen;

n += dtfl_put_i64(buf + n, -3);
off = dtfl_type_tuple_offset(t, buf, n, 1, &flen);
printf("%lld\en", (long long)dtfl_get_i64(buf + off));
dtfl_type_fmt(t, stdout, buf, n);	/* ("apple", -3) */
dtfl_type_free(t);
.Ed
.Sh ERRORS
These functions do not return error codes.
They call the panic hook
.Pq Xr dtfl_set_panic_hook 3
when
.Fn dtfl_type_tuple
is given a field other than the last that does not delimit itself,
when
.Fn dtfl_type_vec
is given such an element type, when
.Fn dtfl_type_new
is given a descriptor with
.Fa internal
set, and when a tuple accessor is given a descriptor that is not a
tuple or an index past its last field.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dtfl_put_u64 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_set_panic_hook 3 ,
.Xr dtfl 7
.Sh HISTORY
Rust gets typed records from monomorphisation.
These descriptors replace it.
Hashes are FNV-1a over libdtfl's encodings, so exchange routing is not
bit-compatible with Rust's
.Vt Hashable ;
a cluster is all-libdtfl.
.Sh THREAD SAFETY
Descriptors are immutable and may be shared between threads.
Reference counts are atomic.
.Fn dtfl_type_new
and the composites may be called from any thread.
